{"id":"agents-root","ord":"a0","title":"Agents","desc":"Who can be dispatched, one node per agent.\n\n- **Launch command:** the `command` property is THE EXACT LAUNCH COMMAND — a launcher reads it and runs it verbatim.\n  - A missing node, or a node without `command`, REFUSES the spawn loudly; nobody falls back to a machine default.\n  - Reason: the Fable burn, 2026-08-13, is why this file exists.\n- **Role:** `role` says what the agent is for.\n  - `prop:role=reviewer` lists the review bench.\n  - `prop:role=author` lists who can hold a lane.\n- **Split:** the note keeps the story and the quirks; the properties keep the facts.\n- **Spawn shape:** `kolu create --repo <repo> --worktree <branch> --json -- <command>`\n- When kolu grows a structured launch spec, these properties migrate into it.","changed":"2026-08-19T18:59:50-04:00"}
{"id":"agent-claude-opus","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a0","title":"claude-opus — the author agent","desc":"Claude Code pinned to Opus with the 1M context window (`opus[1m]`), YOLO mode. The default author for dispatched lanes. Verify with the banner: it must say Opus, not the machine default. The `[1m]` suffix is the human's ruling of 2026-08-21 — a lane that runs for hours must not compact itself into amnesia.","changed":"2026-08-21T21:52:55-04:00","custom":{"command":"claude --model opus[1m] --dangerously-skip-permissions","context":"1M — the [1m] suffix, ruled by the human 2026-08-21 (on the Anthropic API Opus 5 is 1M natively; the suffix pins it everywhere and is harmless where it is the default)","role":"author"}}
{"id":"agent-grok","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a1","title":"grok — reviewer","desc":"Grok CLI in always-approve mode.\n\n- Reviews in a split terminal of the author's worktree.\n- Posts one review comment via gh.\n- Never edits, pushes, or merges.\n- **Authoring track record:**\n  - Shipped #64 (home-manager module) and #153 (parallel e2e) as author.\n  - 2026-08-16: its quiet-outline UI authoring attempt was judged bad by the human and discarded wholesale (terminal killed, no commits worth keeping).\n  - **Guidance:** prefer Opus for UI/design-heavy authoring, grok for reviews and infra-shaped authoring.","changed":"2026-08-22T09:38:57-04:00","custom":{"command":"grok --always-approve","role":"reviewer","usage-limit":"2026-08-22 09:40 — the status bar showed 'Weekly limit left: 8%'; the human: 'Don't worry about Grok; I can increase limit' — do NOT re-dispatch grok lanes on a low-limit reading; if a grok session actually dies on the limit, tell the human and wait"}}
{"id":"agent-opencode","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a2","title":"opencode — reviewer","desc":"opencode TUI on its configured model (kimi-k3 via Juspay at last sighting — the config is opencode's own, not spelled here).\n\n- Same reviewer contract as grok.\n- **Quirks:**\n  - Has mislabeled itself \"codex\" in a posted review once; brief it to title reviews with its tool name.\n  - On PR #193 (2026-08-15) its review asserted \"nothing else in docs//website/ enumerates chat rows or _meta fields, so no drift\" — wrong on both counts (grok found both).\n  - Weigh its no-drift claims accordingly.","changed":"2026-08-19T18:59:50-04:00","custom":{"command":"opencode","role":"reviewer"}}
{"id":"agent-claude-fable","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a3","title":"claude-fable — design-grade author","desc":"Claude Code pinned to Fable (the Mythos-tier model above Opus), YOLO mode. Added 2026-08-19 on the human's word, for design-first work (first use: the vault-in-browser design doc).\n- Reserve for work needing that level — it is the expensive tier; Opus stays the default author.\n- Verify with the banner: it must say Fable, not the machine default.","created":"2026-08-19T20:04:37-04:00","custom":{"command":"claude --model fable --dangerously-skip-permissions","role":"author"}}
{"id":"supervision-watcher","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a4","title":"Supervision: the watcher and the mute list","desc":"The wake mechanism (per instructions.md): `kolu watch --states waiting,awaiting --held-for 60s --nag 10m --ignore-self --heartbeat 30m` run under the harness's Monitor tool with `persistent: true` (a background Bash task notifies only on exit — a watch stream never exits; RCA 2026-08-21).\n\nThe mute list, as `--ignore` flags — fail-open (a stale id costs nothing; every NEW terminal still rings), which is what keeps it legal under the never-an-id-list doctrine. Muted 2026-08-21, all explicitly dispositioned as the HUMAN's own sessions: 0cdc41be + a5e17829 + ab047416 (the kolu#2194 handover — the human took that lane over with their own Claude; orchestrator stands down until handed back), aa15d349 (kolu·damn-spring), 3d01a0b3 (merged docs-PR session), 7251ff2b (nixos-config), 1ef72cfc (olai·master chat session), 2080355a. A terminal handed back to the orchestrator is unmuted by re-arming without its flag; a new human session that starts nagging gets muted the same way after its disposition is verified — never on assumption (identify via kolu ls first).\n\nNag discipline (RCA-2, 2026-08-21): a nag on an unchanged block is re-DERIVED, not re-acknowledged — the second nag with no new information means the block is suspect: act on standing authority or escalate it as a standalone question. A dismissal applies to an event, never to a terminal.","created":"2026-08-21T17:30:28-04:00","changed":"2026-08-23T09:27:23-04:00","custom":{"deploy-2026-08-21":"DEPLOYED ~21:20 and then the orchestrator's own process restarted ~21:25 — the watch died loudly both times as designed and was re-armed (bhb2ugljn); the SECOND restart recycled all terminal ids (the kolu skill's warning made real): the A/B experiment terminal died, every lane's terminal prop went stale, the mute list was rewritten. Production kolu now carries #2194; full real-agent verification run 21:28 (test terminal c01109d6).","kolu-ci-fleet-2026-08-22":"ABANDONED 10:41 — Incus unstable: boxes created Ready at 10:00-10:03 were gone from `pu list` (ERR instance not found) within ~30 min, ci-2 mid-e2e; kolu-ci-8 created 10:38 by me (on linux-08) and left unused; kolu-ci-3 (linux-14) still alive but out of use by ruling","kolu-ci-fleet-gist":"https://gist.github.com/srid/143288f346ba71e27cfb54e67173e3b0 — the pu create failures of 2026-08-22 in full (timeline, outputs, raw server transcripts, registry state, questions for the pu owner)","kolu-pr-process":"RULED by the human 2026-08-22 16:15: kolu PRs are taken through KOLU's own process — the author runs kolu's /be skill (.agents/skills/be/SKILL.md in the kolu checkout) instead of our review/refactor round, and CI through kolu's /ci skill (.agents/skills/ci/SKILL.md) instead of our odu recipe; both platforms green before merge; the orchestrator merges on /be done + /ci green. 16:20: the darwin host /ci names (sincereintent) has been REPLACED by ci@petit (--host aarch64-darwin=ci@petit, under /tmp/olai-odu-petit.lock). Olai PRs keep our process. First applied to lane-scli PR 1 (surface-cli-kolu).","mute-list":"RE-KEYED after the kolu deployment of 2026-08-22 ~19:05. Human's own terminals, never supervised: 30f81ddc (olai master claude), d7543299 (olai master claude), 410e6120 (kolu great-profit claude, #2203), 3e079bd3 (kolu great-profit bash), 724a754e (nixos-config grok), a5d75521 / aea990db / f6331d54 (nixos-config bash). NOT muted but OBSERVE-ONLY: bd0a0a9d (the human's kimi-k3 experiment, node experiment-kimi-k3) — its waiting/awaiting events are observation points; the orchestrator never sends it input. Mine: 24b01598 = the surface-cli author.","odu-venue":"RULING 10:50 2026-08-22 (human): kolu-ci-* dead. TWO venues in parallel, each one-run-at-a-time under a local flock: localhost x86_64-linux (/tmp/olai-odu-localhost.lock, --host x86_64-linux=localhost) and ci@petit aarch64-darwin (/tmp/olai-odu-petit.lock, --host aarch64-darwin=ci@petit) — the --host pin is mandatory (bare --platform dials dead kolu-ci boxes from hosts.json). For olai PRs EITHER platform green is the bar; kolu PRs need both. RULED 12:03 (human): olai's GitHub ruleset still requires the nine @x86_64-linux contexts — ADMIN MERGES ARE FINE for a macOS-only-green olai PR (`gh pr merge --squash --admin`); the ruleset is not narrowed. Measurements under the localhost flock. Brief: briefs/ci-venue-change.md.","verification-2026-08-21":"production kolu#2194 FULL TEST with a real agent (c01109d6, 21:28–21:35) — ALL STAGES PASSED: spawn+boot; typed prompt + Enter; READY 42 in 1s; settle → test watch (--held-for 10s) transition at +10s arriving instantly (per-line flush VERIFIED); nag re-ring at exactly +45s and +90s; main watch (--held-for 60s) transition at +60s; second prompt → second transition; screen_text, kolu ls, --ignore mute list, --ignore-self, --heartbeat; loud death + re-arm twice; kill → terminal gone, state-knob watch silent by design (no gone event, per the contract). Orchestrator's verdict on #2194: GOOD — every claim exercised live on the production build; merge-ready from the consumer's seat.","watch-task":"bu4yzawc2 (re-armed 09:27 2026-08-23 with five mutes; bd0a0a9d un-muted to observe the kimi-k3 experiment)"}}
{"id":"experiment-kimi-k3","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a5","title":"Experiment (the human's, 2026-08-23): opencode + kimi-k3 as an implementing agent vs Claude Opus — observe only, compare at the end","doing":true,"created":"2026-08-23T09:27:02-04:00","changed":"2026-08-23T09:27:19-04:00","custom":{"baseline":"Claude Opus[1m] on lane-scli PR 1 (kolu#2205 @kolu/surface-cli): dispatched 16:09, PR open by 17:56 (1h47m), merged 22:10 (6h01m wall incl. kolu's /be gauntlet + two CI platforms + a redeploy stall ~8 min + an orchestrator venue ruling); 31 commits; 0 human interventions, 3 orchestrator rulings (venue ×2, /be process); 1 e2e flake rerun; 0 stop-and-asks. PR 2 (olai) in flight — its numbers will be added.","criteria":"wall-clock to first PR / to green / to merge; commits; human prompts answered (awaiting events); orchestrator/human rulings needed; review findings (must/should/nits) and how many rounds; CI reruns; context used at the end; scope honesty (deferrals, claims vs verified); tool friction (e.g. `pnpm: command not found` outside nix develop at 09:24)","observations":"09:22 first seen awaiting a prompt (a choice list, 4 options — the human answered); 09:24 working: tried pnpm outside the dev shell (not found), then `nix develop -c … pnpm exec tsx proto-surface.ts surface --help`; context 111K (43%)","task":"as seen 09:24: prototyping `kolu surface <verb>` in packages/kolu-cli on top of @kolu/surface-cli (proto-surface.ts; Command.make('surface') with the padi's verbs) — the kolu-cli migration #2205 explicitly left out","terminal":"bd0a0a9d-c9a8-4ed5-87b8-b29df90e0650 (opencode, model kimi-k3 'Build' agent), kolu worktree kolu-surface-cli — the HUMAN drives it; the orchestrator NEVER sends input, only reads"}}
